From: ODAC maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep shared DNS and DHCP outside the ODAC backend lifecycle

The upstream startup and termination paths unconditionally revert DHCP UCI
state and reload/restart shared dnsmasq. Even empty FQDN lists invoke nftset
helpers that delete shared DHCP settings. The periodic client refresh also
launches legacy ipset-to-nftset synchronization, even with empty DNS lists.
ODAC uses administrator-provisioned DNS/DHCP and its own client policy; it
must not own these operations or run the legacy DNS-set synchronization.

Reject configuration needing the omitted DNS integration through a packaged
read-only checker before setup, including direct daemon execution. Preserve
client authentication/revocation and the nds firewall initialization/cleanup.
No upstream authentication or helper script is modified by this patch.

